@bank all
// W3, rec deck: Works texts on the rec deck (rec engineer B's section 15r and the pool leak trace, claude/rec-works).
// TEXTS. rec.shut.<what>: the toast when you tap something a fault has shut (proposed keys for RB2 to wire; the
// fallbacks in the code are RB's first drafts). trace.pool.*: the leak that drips into Deck 5 main storage (wired as
// worksText). trace.symptom.pool: the traced fault's title (S2's traceTitle; {deck} is the drip's deck).

== rec.shut.float
- The float room's shut: the gravity plates are down. Works are on it.
== rec.shut.net
- The net's down. No Lightdisc till Works fix the emitters.
== rec.shut.belays
- Both auto-belays are tagged out. Works are on it.
== rec.shut.belay
- That route's auto-belay is tagged out. Try the other one.
== rec.shut.route
- That route's taped off: a hold's worked loose. Try another colour.
== rec.shut.pool
- The pool's cloudy. Works have a job in for the filters.

== trace.pool.goal
- See where it drips: main storage
== trace.pool.drip
- A slow drip from the ceiling, over the aisle. The pool plant is right above it.
== trace.pool.up
- Take the spine ladder up to the rec deck and read the pool line with the pipe kit.
== trace.symptom.pool
- Water dripping from the ceiling in main storage on Deck {deck}
